Answer: (A) {−2,2}
Why and working: Adding four gives 2<n²≤4. The only possible integer square is four, so both signed square roots occur.
Why not the others: (B) all have squares at most one. (C) includes inadmissible smaller squares. (D) omits the negative root.

Answer: (A) {2}
Why and working: The first interval restricts x≤2 and the second x≥2. The common endpoint is included by both.
Why not the others: (B) 2 is allowed in both. (C) larger values fail the first constraint. (D) gives their union instead of intersection.
